## 5. UI, UX & Styling (Anti-AI Slop)

- **Tailwind CSS Exclusively:** Do not use raw CSS files, SCSS, or inline `style={{ ... }}` attributes.
- **Mobile-First Responsive Design:** Default utility classes target mobile; use `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`, `xl:` for progressive layout enhancement.
- **Accessible Primitives (Shadcn UI & Radix):** Use Radix primitives and Shadcn UI for complex interactive widgets (dialogs, popovers, dropdowns, tooltips, accordions). Ensure proper keyboard navigation and ARIA attributes out of the box.
- **Refined Aesthetics (Anti-AI Slop):**
  - Generous, deliberate whitespace (`gap-4`, `p-6`).
  - Subtle, consistent border radiuses (`rounded-xl` or `rounded-lg`).
  - Cohesive dark/light palette using semantic tokens (`bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `text-muted-foreground`, `border-border`).
  - Tactile micro-interactions (`transition-colors duration-150`, active scale states `active:scale-[0.98]`, subtle hover effects).
  - Use skeleton loaders that mirror actual content layouts instead of generic blocking spinners.

---

## 6. Data Validation, Fetching & Security

- **Zero Trust Input:** Always validate all client inputs (Server Action payloads, Route Handler bodies, URL search params) using **Zod**.
- **Sanitize Client Responses:** Never return raw database records, ORM error objects, or stack traces to the client.
- **Secrets Management:** Access API keys, private tokens, and database connection strings solely via `process.env`. Never expose sensitive secrets with `NEXT_PUBLIC_` prefixes.

```typescript
// ✅ Server Action with Zod Validation
'use server';

import { z } from 'zod';
import { db } from '@/lib/db';
import { revalidatePath } from 'next/cache';

const UpdatePostSchema = z.object({
  id: z.string().cuid(),
  title: z.string().min(3).max(120),
  content: z.string().min(10),
});

export async function updatePostAction(prevState: unknown, formData: FormData) {
  const result = UpdatePostSchema.safeParse({
    id: formData.get('id'),
    title: formData.get('title'),
    content: formData.get('content'),
  });

  if (!result.success) {
    return { error: 'Invalid submission data', issues: result.error.flatten() };
  }

  try {
    await db.post.update({
      where: { id: result.data.id },
      data: { title: result.data.title, content: result.data.content },
    });
    revalidatePath('/posts');
    return { success: true };
  } catch (err) {
    return { error: 'Failed to update post. Please try again.' };
  }
}
```

